{"id": "EUVD-2026-82054", "enisaUuid": "8ce51b4a-d3ff-3a3b-8915-6a6b4f8c00f8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix potential UAF in bpf_netns_link_update_prog\n\nIn bpf_netns_link_update_prog, the checks for old_prog and prog type\nare currently performed locklessly before acquiring netns_bpf_mutex.\nThis creates a race condition that can lead to a UAF issue.\n\nIf two threads concurrently execute BPF_LINK_UPDATE on the same netns\nlink, the following execution path can trigger a UAF:\n\nCPU0                                          CPU1\nbpf_netns_link_update_prog\n  if (old_prog && old_prog != link->prog)\n    return -EPERM;\n                                              bpf_netns_link_update_prog\n                                                if (old_prog && old_prog != link->prog)\n                                                ...\n                                                old_prog = xchg(&link->prog, new_prog);\n                                                bpf_prog_put(old_prog);\n  if (new_prog->type != link->prog->type) <-- trigger UAF\n\nFix this by moving the old_prog and prog->type checks inside the\nnetns_bpf_mutex critical section. Meanwhile, use guard() to simplify\nlock management and avoid all the goto jumping.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d462b5481d77ce7df8a5ff89a699386f00c9214d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdddf3e1493ee973619c154a57071ce67f78598b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79a66fd997d4eecf17302d613194879eb32e0986", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4ce6803df4095777191d800bebc50219b615ca0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/277168cb9d153ce8e9c3f9275670e32ae61b41d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bda86e9f31b9a296b6e64a51c91dc776fc9f613e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/923f559e95b89b33c7e1793b3d8f7f4ec9b2e4b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c5997836381010fc5907b36bc17d3b19407e933"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9prj-6xm5-hxjf", "CVE-2026-90393"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0498c757-ac54-3933-9aec-6f6ea1058d55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "2a968988-10f8-3caa-a1ae-293ee0eddf58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f045a49fee04b5662cbdeaf0838f9322ae8c63a <79a66fd997d4eecf17302d613194879eb32e0986"}, {"id": "41150087-a376-362f-9309-8d753ade8633", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4265cf5a-5f1f-3cc6-a372-36d49ad3086b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "47f7f139-f688-3705-a459-0a9f0a6b50df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "4aedf795-92c0-32cb-bf5c-13f8fe0a4593", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f045a49fee04b5662cbdeaf0838f9322ae8c63a <5c5997836381010fc5907b36bc17d3b19407e933"}, {"id": "5e707f1b-b1b3-3eeb-9cf7-ca67688c9568", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "68700500-7ba4-3323-adce-4bb37dbf1308", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f045a49fee04b5662cbdeaf0838f9322ae8c63a <277168cb9d153ce8e9c3f9275670e32ae61b41d6"}, {"id": "77f91793-98e8-3069-9462-8d953a713e97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f045a49fee04b5662cbdeaf0838f9322ae8c63a <d462b5481d77ce7df8a5ff89a699386f00c9214d"}, {"id": "7876f43e-257c-3418-993d-18dde678192e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "992c702a-0f07-39ce-837e-f340768de77e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f045a49fee04b5662cbdeaf0838f932